An operating system is an intermediate software layer between your software applications or users and your physical hardware. 
It is the heart of the computer and there are multiple operating systems such as; 
-Linux
-Windows 
-MacOS

The main component of Linux operating system is the Linux Kernel 
What does the Linux Kernel do?
Interaction with hardware such as Process management, Memory management, Disk management and Network management is handeled through the Linux Kernel 

On top of the Linux kernel there are some layers; CLI -> System Libraries -> Kernel 

